THIRD-PARTY DATA
----------------

This tool reads public endpoints at runtime. The terms of each source stay with
that source and are not granted by the licence above. The AGPL covers the code
in this repository; it says nothing about who may use the listings, prices, or
photographs the code fetches.

  klook.com    Listing data is Klook's. This project redistributes no Klook
               dataset and ships no harvested catalogue.
               Klook's robots.txt disallows its search endpoint
               (`Disallow: */search/*`). Klook is therefore **off by default**
               and reaching it requires `--ignore-robots`, an explicit
               per-invocation decision by the operator, announced on stderr and
               named in `coverage.robots_override_hosts`. robots.txt is a
               voluntary crawl directive and overriding it for low-volume
               personal research is a call an operator may make for their own
               traffic. It is not a call this project makes on your behalf,
               which is why the flag exists and why it is not the default.
               The override stops at bot protection. Klook's activity detail
               pages return HTTP 403 (Akamai); the flag does not touch them and
               no code here attempts to. If you need Klook data at any volume,
               or for anything commercial, use Klook's partner API — that route
               needs no override at all.

  airbnb.com   Listing data is Airbnb's and its hosts'. Read only through the
               robots-*allowed* `/api/v3/` path with a public frontend key.
               Airbnb's `Disallow: /s/*/*` is enforced even while
               `--ignore-robots` is set for Klook, because the override is
               per-host. This project redistributes no Airbnb dataset.

  viator.com   Reached through Viator's sanctioned Partner API, which requires
               a key the operator creates themselves (`VIATOR_API_KEY`, read
               from the environment, never stored here). Viator's partner
               agreement governs that data.

TEST FIXTURES
-------------

`tests/fixtures/` contains four unedited captured responses (~800 KB) from
Klook and Airbnb, retained so the parsers are tested against what the servers
actually send rather than against a hand-written idea of it — a hand-written
fixture hid a real bug here once. They are commercial listing records: titles,
prices, ratings, review counts and `a0.muscache.com` listing-photo URLs. They
contain no host names, user identifiers, avatars, contact details, or other
personal data, and they are samples for testing, not a dataset for use. They
are not a licence to the underlying content, and the copyright in that content
remains with Klook, Airbnb, and the hosts.

Do not commit this tool's *output* to a public repository. Ranking and
comparing a few hundred listings for a trip you are planning is what this is
for; republishing someone else's catalogue is not.
